[00:10.12]Why did Elizabeth tell Nigel that she was going to the dentist? | 为什么伊丽莎白告诉奈杰尔她要去看牙医？
[00:17.62]I crossed the street to avoid meeting him but he saw me and came running towards me. | 我穿过马路以便避开他，但他看到我并朝我跑过来。
[00:25.25]It was no use pretending that I had not seen him, so I waved to him. | 假装没看见他是没有用的，我只好向他招了招手。
[00:32.56]I never enjoy meeting Nigel Dykes. | 我从来不喜欢遇到奈杰尔·戴克斯。
[00:36.76]He never has anything to do. | 他从来都是无事可做。
[00:40.34]No matter how busy you are, he always insists on coming with you. | 无论你多忙，他总是坚持要陪着你。
[00:47.77]I had to think of a way of preventing him from following me around all morning. | 我必须想办法不让他整个上午缠着我。
[00:54.80]'Hello, Nigel,' I said 'Fancy meeting you here!' | “你好，奈杰尔，真没想到在这儿见到你！”我说。
[01:00.59]'Hi, Elizabeth,' Nigel answered. 'I was just wondering how to spend the morning--until I saw you. | “你好，伊丽莎白，”奈杰尔回答说，“我正不知道怎么消磨这个上午呢，正好见到了你。
[01:10.77]You're not busy doing anything, are you?' | 你不忙吧？”
[01:14.56]'No, not at all,' I answered. 'I'm going to...' | “不忙，一点事儿也没有，”我回答说，“我正要去……”
[01:19.86]'Would you mind my coming with you?' he asked, before I had finished speaking. | “我跟你一起去行吗？”没等我说完他就问道。
[01:26.53]'Not at all,' I lied, 'but I'm going to the dentist.' | “行，”我撒了个谎，“可我要去看牙医。”
[01:32.57]'Then I'll come with you,' he answered. | “那我跟你一起去，”他回答说。
[01:36.02]'There's always plenty to read in the waiting room!' | “候诊室里总有很多东西可读！”
